From 5db2be3f4d4bed2c543e1e181c976ca9e26aa410 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:25:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] metal boot: pending shielded GPU price (7dd3acd's reviewed
 delta) + explicit operator fees on the normal sender

This commit carries 7dd3acd's reviewed change byte for byte (supervisor.js, metal/guest/gsup.mjs,
test/boot-gpu-price.test.mjs, test/registry-advertise-retry.test.mjs) plus one bounded correction, so the
existing approval-gated build template (single-parent child of 9f6d37bd) can build it.

The correction (2026-10-23, metal0 23:10Z: the boot write was refused "insufficient funds" despite a
passing prefund check; the fee actually sent was not observed): sendOperatorTx left gas and fees to viem's
writeContract. In viem 2.53.1 that first asks the node to fill the transaction (eth_fillTransaction), and
WHERE a node fills, viem multiplies the node's maxFeePerGas by 1.2 again - against a node filling
2 x base + tip, ~13.2 mwei at a 5 mwei base fee instead of 7. That is a reproducible SDK failure scenario
and the suspected production cause, not a confirmed production fee (a direct mainnet.base.org probe did not
fill and fell back to 7 mwei; root will verify the next normal send by its receipt). Where no node fills,
nothing changes. Now, inside the same operator queue: estimateFeesPerGas (block + eth_maxPriorityFeePerGas,
no fill), then estimateContractGas from the operator account at exactly those fees (the node's own estimate,
by fill or eth_estimateGas), then writeContract with that gas and those fees explicit; viem keeps
caller-supplied fees and does not multiply them. A failed read or estimate rejects before anything is
signed. Addresses, functions, arguments, the nonce source, the receipt queue and the delegation are
unchanged.

test/operator-fee-path.test.mjs runs the supervisor's own claimSigner/sendOperatorTx/awaitReceipt on real
viem 2.53.1 clients for Base over a recording stub node that fills a HIGHER fee: against it the 7dd3acd
baseline signs 13.2 mwei; the fix signs 7 mwei with the node's fee-capped gas, from the operator, every node
question at the signed fees; failures send nothing; the queue still serializes through receipts.
